# Proje
CV Compatibility: The project is a Next.js app that provide alignment score, suggestions and lack skills with comparing User resume and job posting.

# Technology
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS
- AI SDK v7 + @ai-sdk/google (Gemini)
- Authentication with Zod

# AI SDK Rules
- Use `generateText` / `streamText` ile `Output.object({ schema })` for structured output. Do not use former `generateObject` API.
- Receive model name always in `env.GEMINI_MODEL`, do not write constantly to code.
- Do not rely on your memory for AI SDK APIs. Before writing any code, read the relevant page at https://ai-sdk.dev/docs. If you are unsure which page to consult, search within the https://ai-sdk.dev/llms.txt file.
- For Next.js, follow the instructions provided in AGENTS.md (located at node_modules/next/dist/docs/).

# Security (mandatory)
- AI calls are performed exclusively on the server (via Route Handlers or Server Actions).
- API keys are never exposed to the client; the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix is ​​not used for sensitive values.
- Environment variables are accessed solely through `src/lib/env.ts`.
- All user input is validated on the server using Zod, with enforced length limits.
- User-provided text is kept separate from system instructions (to prevent prompt injection).
- Personal data, such as the contents of a CV, is never logged.
- Do not show technical details to the user on error messages.

# Code style
- Code, variable, and function names are in English. UI text is in English.
- Small, single-responsibility components. Server-side code is located under `src/lib` and `src/app/api`.
